# ShipASO

Read **`AGENTS.md`** at the repo root first. It is the full agent guide: the
skills index, the credential rules, and how to run the engine. This file exists
only to point you there — it is deliberately not a copy, so the two cannot drift
apart.

Two invariants override convenience everywhere in this codebase:

1. **Measured or nothing.** Every displayed number is measured or absent — `—`,
   never a placeholder, never `0` standing in for "unknown". A fabricated number
   is worse than a missing one.
2. **Approval is the terminus.** Nothing here publishes to a store on its own.
   Skills draft copy and *print* push commands; a human runs them. Approving is
   not shipping.

Before any store write, read the "Before any write to a store" section of
`AGENTS.md`. The short version: ask which API key profile owns the app, and
never handle `.p8` key material — it is passed by path, never pasted.

The 29 runbooks live in `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`.
`skills/store-ops/SKILL.md` is the router: it maps a goal to the right skill.
Read the one you need rather than all of them.
